---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout>
    <header class="site-header shell">
        <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Gallery home">
            <span class="brand-symbol" aria-hidden="true">G</span>
            <span>Gallery</span>
            <span class="brand-by">by Kois</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
            <a href="#idea">The idea</a>
            <a href="#install">Install</a>
            <a class="nav-link-github" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
        <section class="hero shell">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> Self-hosted photo delivery</p>
                <h1>The gallery<br />is the delivery.</h1>
                <p class="hero-lede">
                    A quiet, focused home for sending photographs. Run it yourself, keep the originals close, and give every event a link
                    that feels like the work deserves.
                </p>
                <div class="hero-actions">
                    <a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery"
                        >Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                    >
                    <a class="text-link" href="#idea">See the thinking <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                </div>
                <p class="hero-note"><span class="status-mark"></span> Public project · early beta</p>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-art" aria-label="A preview of the Gallery photo delivery interface" role="img">
                <div class="hero-art-label">A / 01 <span>private delivery</span></div>
                <div class="contact-sheet">
                    <div class="contact-sheet-bar"><span>maria-and-pablo / 2026</span><span>36 photographs</span></div>
                    <div class="contact-sheet-grid">
                        <div class="image-surface image-surface-tall"><span>01</span></div>
                        <div class="image-surface image-surface-wide"><span>02</span></div>
                        <div class="image-surface image-surface-small"><span>03</span></div>
                        <div class="image-surface image-surface-small image-surface-cool"><span>04</span></div>
                        <div class="image-surface image-surface-wide image-surface-deep"><span>05</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="contact-sheet-footer">
                        <span>gallery.example.com/g/maria-and-pablo</span><span class="access-dot">private</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hero-caption">The interface stays out of the way.<br /><span>The photographs do the talking.</span></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="manifesto shell" id="idea" aria-label="Product principles">
            <div class="manifesto-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow">The premise</p>
                <p class="manifesto-lede">The tools for delivering photographs should feel like a gallery, not a file transfer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="manifesto-points">
                <div>
                    <span class="point-number">01</span><strong>Own the room</strong><p>
                        Your installation. Your storage. Your relationship with the people viewing the work.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="point-number">02</span><strong>Keep it quiet</strong><p>
                        A clear interface that gives the photograph the first and last word.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="point-number">03</span><strong>Share with intent</strong><p>
                        One private link from a photographer to a client, without the noise of a generic folder.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="workflow section shell">
            <div class="section-heading-row">
                <div>
                    <p class="eyebrow">A small, useful path</p>
                    <h2>From camera roll<br /><span>to a considered link.</span></h2>
                </div>
                <p class="section-aside">
                    Gallery is intentionally focused: prepare the work, publish the work, let people spend time with it.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="workflow-list">
                <article class="workflow-item">
                    <span>01</span><div><h3>Make a gallery</h3><p>Name the event and create a place for the photographs.</p></div><span
                        class="workflow-arrow">↗</span
                    >
                </article>
                <article class="workflow-item">
                    <span>02</span><div>
                        <h3>Bring in the work</h3><p>Upload a batch and see processing progress as browser-ready images are made.</p>
                    </div><span class="workflow-arrow">↗</span>
                </article>
                <article class="workflow-item">
                    <span>03</span><div>
                        <h3>Publish privately</h3><p>Choose a cover and share a revocable link with the people who need it.</p>
                    </div><span class="workflow-arrow">↗</span>
                </article>
                <article class="workflow-item">
                    <span>04</span><div>
                        <h3>Let it breathe</h3><p>Visitors browse a responsive image grid and download originals when they need them.</p>
                    </div><span class="workflow-arrow">↗</span>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="install-section" id="install">
            <div class="shell install-grid">
                <div class="install-copy">
                    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">Your server, your call</p>
                    <h2>One installation.<br /><span>No platform tax.</span></h2>
                    <p>
                        Gallery is built for a photographer who would rather own a small system than rent a large one. SQLite for the
                        metadata. A mounted storage root for the photographs. A documented path from empty server to working gallery.
                    </p>
                    <a class="button button-light" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery/blob/main/deploy/README.md"
                        >Read the setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                    >
                </div>
                <div class="terminal-card" aria-label="Docker Compose installation example">
                    <div class="terminal-top">
                        <span>gallery / local installation</span><span class="terminal-status"><i></i> ready</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="terminal-body">
                        <p><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone github.com/kois-studio/gallery</p>
                        <p><span class="prompt">$</span> cd gallery/deploy</p>
                        <p><span class="prompt">$</span> docker compose up -d</p>
                        <p class="terminal-result">
                            <span class="prompt">→</span> Gallery is running at <strong>your-domain.example</strong>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="status-section section shell" id="status">
            <div class="section-heading-row">
                <div><p class="eyebrow">The first release</p><h2>Enough to deliver.<br /><span>Room to grow.</span></h2></div>
                <p class="section-aside">
                    The project is being tested as a real product, not padded with features for a roadmap screenshot.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="status-grid">
                <article class="status-card status-card-current">
                    <div class="status-card-top"><span class="status-index">01</span><span class="status-label">implemented</span></div><h3>
                        What works now
                    </h3><ul>
                        <li>Local administrator setup</li><li>Batch JPEG, PNG, and WebP upload</li><li>
                            Thumbnail and display derivatives
                        </li><li>Revocable private share links</li><li>Responsive browsing and original downloads</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="status-card">
                    <div class="status-card-top"><span class="status-index">02</span><span class="status-label">being earned</span></div><h3
                    >
                        What comes next
                    </h3><ul>
                        <li>Real event-volume validation</li><li>Backup and restore evidence</li><li>Additional storage adapters</li><li>
                            Selections shaped by real workflow
                        </li><li>Further delivery and branding tools</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="closing shell">
            <p class="eyebrow">A project by Kois</p>
            <h2>Let the work<br /><span>take the space.</span></h2>
            <p>
                Gallery is a focused open-source direction for photographers who want a beautiful delivery without giving up ownership of
                the system underneath.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery"
                    >Follow the build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                ><a class="text-link" href="https://kois.app">About Kois <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer shell">
        <a class="brand" href="#top"
            ><span class="brand-symbol" aria-hidden="true">G</span><span>Gallery</span><span class="brand-by">by Kois</span></a
        ><p>Software for considered delivery · 2026</p><a href="https://github.com/kois-studio/gallery"
            >GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
    </footer>
</Layout>
